    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) leads the charge as our strongest play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Singer. The combination of a favorable park factor and a massive 13% boost from his platoon split makes him a locked-in core piece, while **Bryce Harper** (71.32) follows closely, buoyed by an elite xwOBA profile and a premium slot in the three-hole. Both **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.91) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) are high-efficiency starts today; **Dylan Beavers** in particular sees his value surge due to an excellent park factor and an optimal leadoff spot against Rodriguez, G, making him a critical engine for our runs and stolen base targets. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also projects as an elite utility option, as his platoon advantage and batting order stability create a high floor that forces him into the starting rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Braden Montgomery** (44.00), who hovered near the threshold but ultimately fell short due to a suboptimal eight-hole assignment and a challenging matchup against the lefty Sandoval. While **Gleyber Torres** (42.31) also carried some appeal, the combination of his negative platoon outlook and superior efficiency metrics from our active middle infielders like **Masyn Winn** kept him on the pine. We are monitoring **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.99) closely; his score is hampered by a significant platoon disadvantage against Gore, though his speed profile provides a necessary buffer for our stolen base objectives. Aside from **Will Smith** remaining sidelined on the IL, we have no significant weather flags, though we must continue to watch for late lineup adjustments to ensure **Cal Raleigh** (51.48) and **Yainer Diaz** (54.99) maintain their projected plate appearances.",
